150 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (Before any meaningful analysis can be carried out, raw data must first be organized and cleaned. Real-world datasets frequently contain missing values, inconsistent formatting, and duplicate records, so data cleaning forms a foundational step that determines the reliability of every subsequent stage of analysis. Once cleaned, data can be explored using tools such as Microsoft Excel for spreadsheet-based analysis, Python together with the Pandas library for programmatic data manipulation, and business intelligence platforms such as Power BI for building dashboards and calculated business measures that communicate findings to stakeholders. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
151 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (This report documents a six-week internship in the Data Analyst domain undertaken with BeeSkilled, during which these concepts were studied and applied through four weekly modules: Excel-based sales analysis, Python/Pandas-based dataset exploration, Python- based data wrangling and cleaning, and a concluding data-visualization and business- analytics capstone project. The internship provided an opportunity to connect the theoretical foundation gained through the B.Tech CSE curriculum with practical, hands-on data analysis work, and to understand how raw business data is progressively transformed into decision-ready insight. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
