/T (The Week 1 assignment involved building a pivot-table-based analysis of sales performance from the "Global Superstore" Orders dataset, which contained approximately 51,290 records across 24 columns. Category-wise sales, shown in Figure 4.2, were led by Technology at approximately $4.74M, followed by Furniture at approximately $4.11M and Office Supplies at approximately $3.79M. Yearly sales showed a consistent upward trend, rising from approximately $2.26M in 2012 to approximately $4.30M in 2015. )
/E (The Week 1 assignment involved building a pivot-table-based analysis of sales performance from the "Global Superstore" Orders dataset, which contained approximately 51,290 records across 24 columns. Category-wise sales, shown in Figure 4.2, were led by Technology at approximately $4.74M, followed by Furniture at approximately $4.11M and Office Supplies at approximately $3.79M. Yearly sales showed a consistent upward trend, rising from approximately $2.26M in 2012 to approximately $4.30M in 2015. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [25]
>>
